  "worked_solution": "First, we differentiate $x(y)$ with respect to $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(\\frac{2}{y}+\\frac{8}{{y}^{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}(2{y}^{-1}+8{y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-1})+8\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}y}({y}^{-2}) \\\\  & =2\\cdot (-{y}^{-2})+8\\cdot (-2{y}^{-3}) \\\\  & =-2{y}^{-2}-16{y}^{-3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{{y}^{2}}-\\frac{16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2y-16}{{y}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2y+16}{{y}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, taking the reciprocal of $\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={(\\frac{\\text{d}x}{\\text{d}y})}^{-1}=-\\frac{{y}^{3}}{2y+16}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the point $(3,2),$ we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}{|}_{(x,y)=(3,2)} & =-\\frac{{2}^{3}}{2(2)+16} \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{20} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
